course: dictionary
lesson: 10837
title: Painting with words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your head, and verdant is one of them. It is a formal word, found mostly in poems and stories, and it means green and full of growing plants and grass. In The Wind in the Willows, the Rat wanders «by the verdant banks of dream-rivers», so the banks are green and covered in plants.
explain: Check the clues around the word. Banks and rivers are places where plants grow, and the picture is one of fresh, rich green. Try swapping in "green" and see if the sentence still makes sense: "the green banks of dream-rivers" works, so you have understood it.
explain: Verdant is a describing word, an adjective, like «verdant hills» or «verdant meadows». Its describing phrase tells the reader what the hills or meadows look like. It can also change: more verdant, most verdant.
explain: Wet places are often verdant. In geography, Ireland's wet climate helps make its land verdant, so its fields and hills look green and full of plants. Writers choose verdant when they want the reader to see that fresh green.
fact: Verdant means green and full of growing plants and grass.
fact: Verdant is a formal, literary word, so you will meet it most in poems and stories.
fact: «Verdant meadows» and «verdant hills» are describing phrases: verdant tells you what the meadows and hills look like.
fact: Verdant is an adjective, and it has the forms more verdant and most verdant.
fact: In geography, wet climates such as Ireland's can make the land verdant.
exercise: «He wandered by the verdant banks of dream-rivers.» What does verdant mean here? | Cold and icy | Loud and busy | *Green and full of growing plants | Dry and dusty
exercise: Which of these would a writer most likely describe as verdant? | A dark, empty cave | A frozen lake | *Rolling hills covered in fresh green grass | A busy motorway
exercise: «The verdant meadows stretched far away.» Find and copy the describing word that tells you the meadows are green. | far | *verdant | away | stretched
test: According to the lesson, what kind of climate can make land verdant? | *A wet climate, such as Ireland's | A dry, sandy climate | A freezing climate with heavy snow | A climate with no rain at all
test: Which word is closest in meaning to verdant? | Icy | Parched | Barren | *Lush
exam: «The verdant hills were full of sheep.» Verdant is a describing word, so what does it tell you about the hills? | How tall they are only | Their name | How old they are | *Their green colour and the plants growing on them
